{"name":"Rhododendron","hex":"#7d2f45","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Rhododendron","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Ericaceae – rhododendrons and azaleas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Rhododendron"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rhododendron","blocks":[{"text":"Rhododendron, from Ancient Greek ῥόδον (rhódon), meaning \"rose\", and δένδρον (déndron), meaning \"tree\", is a very large genus of about 1,024 species of woody plants in the heath family (Ericaceae). They can be either evergreen or deciduous. Most species are native to eastern Asia and the Himalayan region, but smaller numbers occur elsewhere in Asia, and in North America, Europe and Australia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Alpenroos.jpg/330px-Alpenroos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhododendron"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/%D0%9D%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%89%D1%96_%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%96_%D0%B6%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%82%D1%8F.jpg/500px-%D0%9D%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%89%D1%96_%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%96_%D0%B6%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%82%D1%8F.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/%D0%9D%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%89%D1%96_%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%96_%D0%B6%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%82%D1%8F.jpg/1280px-%D0%9D%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%89%D1%96_%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%96_%D0%B6%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%82%D1%8F.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/%D0%9D%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%89%D1%96_%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%96_%D0%B6%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%82%D1%8F.jpg/500px-%D0%9D%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%89%D1%96_%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%96_%D0%B6%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%82%D1%8F.j